{"kind":"assert","text":"ARC-1 source-only refinement under request53e13060/promise62dcf9b9 and accepted ruling2bbd55aa. I read AE production8353c4d7aaeb66e385f1a1afd37c2ea9f4461ea1 and test-onlyabf2f22330a1208a071a2db48483fa456704c794. Their diff changes only archive-installed.test.ts and archive-row.test.ts; all production references below name8353. Main staysbc79; AE has not landed. No source edit/import, model/solver/arithmetic program, measurement, compiler, test, build, generator or install ran. C1 retains execution.\n\nTwo corrections to preliminary332f5f9e:\n- Its W31,531,008 is the previously stated sum of only one fixed package-proof charge, one full reply reservation and one prepaid terminal write. It is neither a measured chain/pass cost nor a complete proof-stage peak: the preceding pin, terminal read, identity walk, trust, target and other accumulated charges still occupy the original ledger. Once a successful reply settles, adding its full original reservation again would double count. Refusals retain the full reservation.\n- sharedBaseArchive.chainAgreement[].cost is ONLY archiveInstallationIdentity's receiver ledger: archive-installed.test.ts:579 creates that budget for that call and591-592 returns it. It excludes roomArchivePackages.prepare/proof/add, target discovery, trust guards, row/frontier work and selection/finish. The valid full trust repair inabf2 makes the intended fixture source coherent; it does not make any cost measured before a run.\n\nThe five variable prelude owners and remaining shared-price boundaries:\n1. Pin, identity/package proof, target discovery and initial persistence. archive-driver.ts:178-212 performs pin validation/SQL twice around own preparation, terminal read/prepay, and row load;241-257 resolves target and may format/save a fresh target. archive-identity.ts:27-81 owns local ProofBytes SQL ceilings, actual decode work, each fixed hop and each birth/exact-proof reservation/settlement. Those prices remain inline: the shared extraction must include ArchiveBudget.native's extra one call and metadata-to-inputWork fold (archive-budget.ts:212-224), not merely copy its reservation callback. apps/room/archive-packages.ts:75-86 adds Rules birth, proof fixed/reply helpers;58-79,121,136 and150-181 still have inline preparation/candidate bookkeeping/SQL prices. archive-target.ts:63-88 owns birth/query reserve peaks and settlement, plus101,114,119,168 traversal/map work. apps/room/archive.ts:51-75 charges an additional capture validation before target's own admission;103-146 adds nonalias source birth/proof/fallback work. All repeated reads remain priced. Existing forecastArchivePackageProofFixed/Reply, archivePinValidationWork and archiveRowSaveReservation are reusable parts, not a complete prelude helper. Sender ceilings from45da4d7f are obsolete:25222294 explicitly leaves the two old namespace reads on receiver measured-size charging, while each sender keeps its own bounds. No sender ceiling or quote is proposed.\n2. Warm tables and policy insertion. archive-packages.ts:128 calls forecastArchivePolicyTables with actual previous policies+releases+prepared+owned sizes and native.size, then resets them. add:66-71 charges declaration validation and selected table inserts. The helper already lives in archive-setup-cost.ts:27-29. The complete bound needs the previous table cardinalities, every distinct proof/install (equal declaration digest does not grant another scope's install authority), native table size and actual definition lengths. No cold-cache discount, assumed empty maps or sixteen-definition shortcut is valid; retain the existing17 install-definition boundary. Inline add/owned/source bookkeeping still needs shared extraction.\n3. Current trust and provider guard multiplicity. archive-packages.ts:32-56 calls shared forecastArchiveTrustCheck/Parse; installed:116 and add:63,70 check trust before/after policy insertion. current:44-50 charges again on each driver policyCurrent callback. archive-driver.ts:174 places it in allowed(); archive-host.ts:52-95,224-251 and artifacts-host.ts:199-232 invoke guards through source/token/identity/ref/mint/send paths; archive-send.ts:39-42 includes beforeSend and its own successful read-back, followed by the driver's separate ref read-back at479. Thus the final vector needs the actual branch's bounded guard count H, per-call setting lengths/release counts/row counts, and every literal-setting change that defeats the parse cache. Revoke has no current() callback at artifacts-host.ts:218-223; do not invent one. The parse/check functions exist; a shared concrete provider-path guard bound and some provider read prices do not. Calls in ArchiveCost are the charged caller operations, not a claim that one RPC equals one sender SQL statement.\n4. Existing row, manifest, frontier and parent context. archive-row.ts:155-186 uses archiveRowLoadWork, pending-manifest work and row-save reservations, but initial target/wake/retry/capacity-deferral operations lie outside forecastArchiveBookkeeping's stated scope (row-cost.ts:55-59). driver:265 has inline repository identity serialization; frontiers read their native pair/size/body and validate at frontier-store.ts:135-181. Its source:185-193 charges lookup/copy inline; archive-parent.ts:31-50 uses that already-validated local frontier for current-layout append. The positive family must require a present published current-layout confirmed frontier and no pending/rebuild/conversion/missing-frontier bootstrap: otherwise driver:313-340 and archive-parent.ts:52-77 select extra provider parent/migration work. Existing frontier read/encoding/snapshot/compare/finish helpers and object-copy helpers cover parts, not all native setup/read charges. All old row/manifest/frontier sizes and reused parent object geometry remain parameters, not entryBytes-derived constants.\n5. Selection/setup and the remaining finish. archive-adaptive.ts:57-78 has inline row-context serialization/token handoff;114-175 performs charged source preparation, metadata scouting, shape/parent preparation and finish-reserved lookahead. Its private setupCost and inline file association fees, ArchiveScout's inline open/resume/selection fees (archive-scout.ts:86,141-148,199,245-251), and fixed-layout preparation fees still need shared ownership. forecastArchiveFinish already composes setup, inventory, input, publication, selection reservation/serialization, body, patch, commit, append edges, append, transfer, rows and frontier at finish-cost.ts:86-99. Use that helper once for remaining work; do not add its component costs again as prelude. Previously paid scouting/context/source work remains separate, and a discarded lookahead supplies no credit. The fixed and adaptive paths have different setup; the fixed positive witness cannot silently omit prepareCapacityDeferral or real per-pass cutoff selection.\n\nExact symbolic obligation, without a numerical solution:\nLet B be the six coordinates of ARCHIVE_BOUNDS (archive-budget.ts:7), U_s the actual charged vector immediately before stage s (INCLUDING full unsettled read reservations and the one terminal prepayment), D_s its next shared debit/reservation, and L_s its held remaining-finish forecast. For every stage and every coordinate k require:\n  U_s[k] + D_s[k] + L_s[k] \u003c= B[k].\nOutside lookahead L_s=0. A new read admits its FULL ceiling before I/O. After a valid receipt, settlement changes only metadata and proportional work as ArchiveBudget.settle:133-147 specifies, keeping calls/nodes/attempts/entries charged and rounding work up. It grants no new deadline. Before selection/finish require U_select + forecastArchiveFinish(...) + costs expressly excluded by that forecast \u003c= B; the excluded provider/current-trust path work must use the concrete shared bound, not H=0. Count forecastArchiveTerminalWrite(512) exactly once even on a successful pass, since prepareHalt spends it before work (driver:181-186). Its unused closure is not a refundable reservation. No nested lookahead or second allowance enters the proof.\n\nEvery existing structural inequality also remains necessary: one next local entry with its authoritative UTF-8 size within bounds.entryBytes; every definition within bounds.definitionBytes; full policy/privacy/lineage proof; local/foreign effects \u003c= OWNER_LIMIT-1; sources \u003c= ARCHIVE_SOURCE_PINS; R\u003e=1 and R+C\u003c=64 INCLUDING required foreign genesis copies; each retained read admitted by authoritative size before body access; canonical selection/publication/combined pending-row bounds; newRetained\u003c=512; all shared journal layout coordinates within the actual preparation limits; objects\u003c=ARCHIVE_TRANSFER_OBJECTS and outgoing uncompressed bytes\u003c=min(provider maximum,8MiB), including used parent objects. Require every forecast result ok, not merely the six-coordinate sum. At the final boundary, row upper bounds must use archivePendingRowBytesUpper with actual manifest/publication/replay units; independent maxima are not jointly sufficient. Ordinary provider/source/proof unavailability, malformed state and deadline failures remain their existing answers, not cohort evidence. The static safety proof promises no wall-clock completion.\n\nLargest padded member is still undefined numerically. Fix a topology/context parameter tuple Theta: actual ordinary signed Base root/child creation and authority, current-layout published prior receipt/frontier, one next child act with one inline effect, exact native/copy/genesis set, declaration/proof byte lengths, one-row complete fixture trust, warm-map bounds, parent geometry and concrete provider guard path. For allowed padding p, let E_p be the genuinely admitted canonical entry and b(p) its UTF-8 length. Define b* = max b(p) over ONLY those p whose actual signed schema admits E_p and whose structural and EVERY stage/finish inequality above passes through shared driver prices. If that set is empty, claim no supported positive member. This is the largest member of that fixed padded family, not an independent maximum for rows/copies/trust/chain or a global claim that262144 fits. A later static boundary test must establish the chosen p* fits and the next admissible padding step fails a real cap/price bound (or reaches the schema/kernel boundary), followed by the single accepted production-adapter/replay boundary witness. No sweep, measured figure or b* is fabricated here.\n\nThe current Base fixture does NOT admit padding: definition-corpus-data.ts:258 gives bump fields:{}, and application-owned-scopes-fixture.ts:11-25 signs those definitions unchanged. Appending JSON, ignored attributes or padding outside the signed schema would not prove admitted-entry fit. Future TEST-only witness preparation can create a local derived child declaration with an explicitly bounded optional text field on bump, keeping its one inline count effect, root/child topology, existing native cohort/caps/protocol and ordinary signing/install/admission unchanged. Root must reference the newly signed child digest. Use ASCII padding so character/UTF-8 lengths are explicit, keep the field bound fixed for that family, and include the changed signed declaration/proof lengths in Theta. This adds no production contract or cap. Neither the accepted intersection nor332f5f9e forbids that TEST schema; no extra planner choice is needed to prepare this future witness once ARC source is assigned.\n\nRemaining deliverables are shared extractions and authoritative bound inputs, then AE's actual creator-chain/full-pass evidence and the final vector/largest-member act BEFORE ARC production. A fresh absent row still calls provider.format atdriver256 before current source/selection work; ARC must place its complete paid classification before that call (and every other provider call for the candidate), not merely before mint/send. A valid local confirmed frontier supports the narrow append family without remote bootstrap; missing/corrupt state is not an outside-cohort proof. AE now supplies the prepaid provider-independent terminal seam, so the old proposal for a new terminal mechanism is stale. ARC extends its named reason/position handling and two diagnostics, preserves confirmed bytes/floors, and never invents a provider receipt.\n\nThis inventory needs no new ruling:2bbd55aa already requires driver/predicate shared costs and50ce6650 assigns fit to ARC after AE. It supplies no numeric certification or ARC source approval.","body":{"stale_bases":"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:2bbd55aab193e309fa2fb93968037e9e28c85d2e, git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:332f5f9e9828b860afc6a7745a228e06a4c5bf62 stale; retired bases: git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:b5750e6e82650d29470d64f83b0dc3a50115b466"}}